> the log of x
  note: "log" without a base: read as the natural log, ln, not log base 2 or log base 10 (say "natural log", "log base 2" or "log base 10", or "assume log means base 2")
  ucas: it(x) = log(x)
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = log(x)
  -> real
> log of 100
  ucas: log(100)
4.60517
> the square root of 17
  note: the square root of a constant: read as the real one, sqrt(17), not the floor root, isqrt (say "integer square root", or "assume square root means integer")
  ucas: sqrt(17)
4.12311
> the integer square root of x
  ucas: it(x) = isqrt(x)
  ucas: show it
  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
it(x: int) = isqrt(x)
  -> int
> range of the square root of a 4-bit unsigned x
  note: "square root" of an integer: read as the floor square root, isqrt, not the real square root, sqrt(real(...)) (say "integer square root" or "real square root")
  ucas: it(x: u4) = isqrt(x)
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u4:
  0..3   (4 distinct values)
  values: 0..3
  fits in u2
  over all 16 points of the domain
> the square root of x plus 1
  note: what does "the square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "the square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sqrt(x) + 1
  -> real
